{
  "language": "csharp",
  "extensions": [".cs"],
  "kinds": {
    "func": [
      { "type": "method_declaration" },
      { "type": "constructor_declaration" }
    ],
    "class": [
      { "type": "class_declaration" },
      { "type": "interface_declaration" },
      { "type": "struct_declaration" }
    ],
    "interface": [
      { "type": "interface_declaration" }
    ],
    "struct": [
      { "type": "struct_declaration" }
    ],
    "enum": [
      { "type": "enum_declaration" }
    ],
    "namespace": [
      { "type": "namespace_declaration" }
    ],
    "var": [
      { "type": "variable_declaration" },
      { "type": "field_declaration" }
    ],
    "comment": [
      { "type": "comment" }
    ]
  },
  "notes": "El modificador 'const' de C# vive dentro de un nodo 'modifier' hermano, no un hijo directo del campo — demasiado profundo para requires_child_type — por eso los campos const también se filtran bajo 'var'."
}
